# Operator replies

User-facing replies are for the operator. Routing notes, model lists, and other internal tool lines stay hidden.

Codex Speeder is a user-facing product. The chat line is for the operator. Speeder JSON and skill internals stay compact.

- Chat: one `↳ Codex Speeder:` line about what it saved them (files picked, or reused last lookup). Never say "skipped".
- Do not paste Speeder JSON, `user_summary`, cache, or routing into the chat.
- Put the work result (deploy, revision, positions, SQL) in the main answer, never in the Speeder line.
- Lead with the answer: what is true, what changed, or what to do next.
- Use the same words the operator used (deploy, positions, SQL, revision).
- Hide internal status such as `workflow-saver`, `STATUS: APPROVE`, `CACHE_HANDOFF`, or participating models.

```text
Bad Speeder:  ↳ Codex Speeder: already has this deploy path; FULL revision is healthy
Bad Speeder:  ↳ Codex Speeder: skipped, already known; continue with the current file and test
Good Speeder: ↳ Codex Speeder: found the 3 files this change needs
Good Speeder: ↳ Codex Speeder: reused last file list; no extra repo scan
```
